<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Deliberately empty. A free Apple ID team cannot hold an App Group, and the team
	     provisioning profiles it issues carry `application-groups` as an empty array — so an
	     entitlements file that asks for `group.ie.shoonya.yantra` is refused outright with
	     "doesn't match the entitlements file's value". This is the device twin of the real
	     entitlements: same file, no group.

	     What that costs, and why it is survivable: the widgets and the share extension cannot see
	     the workspace on a device build, and `Diagnostics` writes to the app's own Documents
	     directory rather than the shared container for exactly this reason. On the simulator the
	     real entitlements are used and both work. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
